  "summary": "An SFPD audit found that NCRIC and the West States Information Network improperly accessed San Francisco's Flock ALPR data hundreds of times, including queries on behalf of out-of-state agencies, in apparent violation of California's 2015 law restricting ALPR data sharing. SFPD has since disabled NCRIC and WSIN access; Secure Justice plans to sue, while SFPD says no ICE or DHS access has been identified.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "San Francisco's license plate reader data has been improperly accessed hundreds of times by out-of-state and federal agencies since last May, police officials said Wednesday.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Under a 2015 state law, California public agencies are barred from sharing license plate reader data with federal and out-of-state agencies",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "The department has since disabled both NCRIC and WSIN's access to the city's camera network",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "It involved searches conducted by authorized users at a California state agency that were later determined to be inconsistent with California's ALPR data-sharing requirements.",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    }
  ],
